<article class="env-theorem" id="945046">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/945046">Theorem <span data-tag="945046">2.4.6.1</span>.</a>$\infty $-category!as a fibrant object of $\sSet $ Let $\calC $ be a simplicial set. Then $\calC $ is fibrant for the Joyal model structure if and only if $\calC $ is an $\infty $-category. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof of Theorem <a href="/tag/945046" data-tag="945046">2.4.6.1</a>.</strong>
       The “only if” direction has already been established (Remark <a href="/tag/A863E1" data-tag="A863E1">2.2.5.5</a>). For the converse, we must show that if $\calC $ is an $\infty $-category, then $\calC $ has the extension property with respect to every inclusion of simplicial sets $A \subseteq B$ which is a categorical equivalence. Fix any map $A \rightarrow \calC $. Since the Joyal model structure is left-proper, the inclusion $\calC \subseteq \calC \coprod _{A} B$ is a categorical equivalence. We now apply Lemma <a href="/tag/2F816F" data-tag="2F816F">2.4.6.4</a> to conclude that $\calC $ is a retract of $\calC \coprod _{A} B$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>